cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this study, please cite it as below. Please also cite C²KV
  (Du et al., KDD 2026), whose published mechanism this repository reimplements
  and measures.
title: "context-cache-lab: a C²KV-style replication and measurement study of composable compiled context state on Apple Silicon"
abstract: >-
  A negative-result-preserving research repository testing whether long LLM
  context can be compiled once into compact, independently generated, composable
  model-readable state that a frozen target model can consume in place of the
  original tokens. Stage 1 established a clean native baseline on a deterministic
  synthetic corpus (NATIVE 0.947 vs NOCTX 0.000). Stage 2a found that
  training-free KV thinning collapses even at 2x, while equal-budget raw text
  degrades as roughly 1/r. Stage 2b trained a 566M-parameter C2KV-style sidecar
  over a frozen Qwen3-4B and found that learned compressed state beat
  equal-position raw context at every ratio tested, with semantic facts surviving
  far better than hashes and identifiers, and warm reuse 23-32x faster than native
  prefill (breakeven at 2 queries); its preregistered gate nevertheless returned
  INCONCLUSIVE. Stage 3 evaluated that frozen carrier on a preregistered
  cross-page compositional task and it FAILED, scoring zero clean accuracy on all
  native-valid two-page items. The general composable-page claim is therefore not
  supported by these measurements.
type: software
